@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# ADR-0006: Carry declared native accessibility actions through AT-SPI
+
+- Status: accepted in the owner fork; native integration verification in progress
+- Date: 2026-10-30
+
+## Decision
+
+Retain React Native's accessibilityActions and onAccessibilityAction contract.
+Expose each declared label through the real AT-SPI Action interface and deliver
+its declared name with ViewEventEmitter::onAccessibilityAction on the frame
+thread. Recheck current declarations, handler presence, disabled state, role,
+emitter identity and hidden ancestors before dispatch. Custom actions do not
+synthesize a pointer gesture or silently acquire focus.
+
+AccessKit's current Unix translation exposes only click. Carry a small patch of
+its exact accesskit_atspi_common 0.21.1 crate in this fork. Fetch the registry
+archive by the existing C ABI Cargo.lock checksum, preserve its licenses, apply
+the transport patch and use Cargo's path override. Both fetched sources live in
+the same FetchContent dependency directory; the C ABI manifest names its sibling.
+The lockfile patch removes source/checksum only for that exact overridden crate.
+Keep --locked for builds. Other dependency versions retain the pinned lockfile.
+Use forward-only patching and disconnected updates for the pinned C ABI checkout
+so repeated CMake configuration preserves the manifest and lockfile override.
+
+Custom IDs remain stable while an action name is declared. Removed IDs are never
+reassigned to another name in that session. Immutable publications carry the
+mapping; worker callbacks read it and queue bounded requests. Frame-only ID
+assignment never reaches Fabric, Wayland or JSI from a Rust callback thread.
+
+## Verification
+
+Three production-adapter tests fail before the Rust transport patch. All ten
+crate tests pass afterward, covering names, opaque IDs, default click coexistence,
+invalid indices, disabled state, changes and removal. A Linux-filtered --locked
+Cargo metadata check resolves one copy each of accesskit, its consumer, Unix and
+the patched common crate. The C++ owner/snapshot tests and actual packed native
+application must also pass, including real external AT-SPI calls and lifecycle
+sanitizers, before this feature is described as verified.
+
+Clean the generated native build directory after editing dependency patches so
+FetchContent populates and patches fresh source. No dependency or original-project
+PR is created by this integration.
